---
import SiteHead from "../components/SiteHead.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const standards = [
  { label: "Sources", href: "#sources" },
  { label: "Verification", href: "#verification" },
  { label: "AI use", href: "#ai-use" },
  { label: "Corrections", href: "#corrections" },
  { label: "Commercial independence", href: "#commercial-independence" },
] as const;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <SiteHead
      title="Research & Standards | Portfilo"
      description="How Portfilo handles sourcing, verification, AI use, corrections, and commercial independence."
    />
  </head>
  <body class="editorial-page">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#standards-content">Skip to standards</a>

    <SiteHeader current="standards" />

    <main id="standards-content" tabindex="-1">
      <header class="standards-header" aria-labelledby="standards-title">
        <div class="standards-header__copy">
          <p class="standards-kicker">Research / Standards</p>
          <h1 id="standards-title">How Portfilo works with evidence.</h1>
          <p class="standards-intro">
            We use reporting, documents, data, and other evidence to establish what a
            story can support. These standards explain how we source information,
            verify important claims, use AI, correct errors, and keep commercial
            interests separate from editorial conclusions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <nav class="standards-index" aria-label="Research and standards sections">
          <p>On this page</p>
          <ul>
            {standards.map((item) => <li><a href={item.href}>{item.label}</a></li>)}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <div class="standards-sections">
        <section class="standard-section" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
          <div class="standard-section__heading">
            <p class="standard-section__label">Sources</p>
            <h2 id="sources-title">Start as close to the evidence as possible.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="standard-section__body">
            <p>We prefer primary sources when they are available: official datasets, laws and regulations, company filings and records, peer-reviewed research, original datasets, direct interviews, official documentation, transcripts, and records created by the event being reported.</p>
            <p>Independent reporting and research can provide corroboration, context, and facts that cannot be reconstructed from primary material. Market platforms, surveys, social posts, and community discussions can also be useful, but we examine what they can actually establish before relying on them.</p>
            <p>A person or company saying something proves that they made the claim. It does not automatically prove that the underlying claim is true.</p>
            <div class="standard-note">
              <p class="standard-note__label">Source principle</p>
              <p>Relevance and methodology matter more than a source label alone.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="standard-section" id="verification" aria-labelledby="verification-title">
          <div class="standard-section__heading">
            <p class="standard-section__label">Verification</p>
            <h2 id="verification-title">Important claims have to survive a skeptical check.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="standard-section__body">
            <p>Consequential factual claims are checked against their underlying evidence. Before publication, we audit material numbers, dates, names, titles, quotations, company claims, legal or regulatory claims, and other assertions where an error could change the story.</p>
            <p>We also look for evidence that challenges the emerging conclusion. Competing datasets, different methodologies, selection bias, weak causal reasoning, stale information, and financially interested sources can all change what a story should say.</p>
            <p>If the evidence is incomplete, we qualify the claim, explain the limitation when it matters, continue reporting, or remove the claim. We do not turn missing evidence into false precision.</p>
            <div class="standard-note">
              <p class="standard-note__label">Unsupported material</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Find evidence</li>
                <li>Qualify the statement</li>
                <li>Remove it</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="standard-section" id="ai-use" aria-labelledby="ai-title">
          <div class="standard-section__heading">
            <p class="standard-section__label">AI use</p>
            <h2 id="ai-title">AI can help with the work. It cannot establish the facts.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="standard-section__body">
            <div class="standard-subsection">
              <h3>AI may assist with</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>finding research leads and possible sources;</li>
                <li>organizing and summarizing documents;</li>
                <li>comparing sources and identifying contradictions;</li>
                <li>calculation or code assistance;</li>
                <li>developing questions, drafts, and edits after the writing form is chosen;</li>
                <li>skeptical review that points to claims needing another check.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="standard-subsection">
              <h3>AI cannot substitute for</h3>
              <ul>
                <li>a source;</li>
                <li>evidence;</li>
                <li>verification;</li>
                <li>reporting;</li>
                <li>editorial authority for structure, voice, or institutional claims;</li>
                <li>authority for a quotation, statistic, attribution, law, or current fact.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="standard-note">
              <p>Factual material surfaced by AI must be independently checked before it can be published. AI output is not treated as authority for how a story should be structured or how Portfilo should describe itself.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="standard-section" id="corrections" aria-labelledby="corrections-title">
          <div class="standard-section__heading">
            <p class="standard-section__label">Corrections</p>
            <h2 id="corrections-title">Material factual errors are corrected visibly.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="standard-section__body">
            <p>When a consequential factual error is found, we correct the story and attach a visible correction note. The note should state the correction date, what was wrong, and what is correct.</p>
            <p>We do not silently rewrite a material error in a way that hides the correction. Minor typographical or formatting fixes do not require a formal correction unless they change meaning.</p>
            <div class="standard-note">
              <p class="standard-note__label">Correction record</p>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>Date</dt><dd>When the correction was made</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Wrong</dt><dd>What the story previously said</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Correct</dt><dd>What the evidence supports</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="standard-section" id="commercial-independence" aria-labelledby="commercial-title">
          <div class="standard-section__heading">
            <p class="standard-section__label">Commercial independence</p>
            <h2 id="commercial-title">A commercial relationship cannot determine the factual conclusion.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="standard-section__body">
            <p>Sponsors, advertisers, partners, and affiliates may not determine the factual conclusion of Portfilo editorial coverage.</p>
            <p>Commercial material must be clearly labeled. Advertising should not be presented as independent reporting. If a commercial relationship is relevant to how a reader would interpret a story, it should be disclosed.</p>
            <div class="standard-note">
              <p class="standard-note__label">Editorial rule</p>
              <p>Commercial support does not buy an editorial conclusion.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />

    <style>
      :global(html) {
        scroll-behavior: smooth;
      }

      .standards-header,
      .standards-sections {
        width: min(calc(100% - (2 * var(--shell-gutter))), var(--content-max));
        margin-inline: auto;
      }

      .standards-header {
        padding: clamp(2.8rem, 2rem + 2.6vw, 5.4rem) 0 clamp(2.4rem, 2rem + 1.8vw, 4rem);
      }

      .standards-header__copy {
        max-width: 54rem;
      }

      .standards-kicker,
      .standard-section__label,
      .standard-note__label,
      .standard-subsection h3,
      .standards-index > p {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font: 550 0.72rem/1.35 var(--sans);
        letter-spacing: 0.07em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      .standards-kicker {
        color: var(--accent);
      }

      .standards-header h1 {
        max-width: 13ch;
        margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
        font: 650 clamp(2.55rem, 1.35rem + 3vw, 4.7rem) / 0.96 var(--sans);
        letter-spacing: -0.055em;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }

      .standards-intro {
        max-width: 43rem;
        margin: clamp(1.3rem, 2.2vw, 1.9rem) 0 0;
        font: 400 clamp(1.04rem, 0.96rem + 0.25vw, 1.2rem) / 1.65 var(--serif);
      }

      .standards-index {
        margin-top: clamp(2.2rem, 3.5vw, 3.4rem);
        padding: 0.85rem 0;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 0.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 1.5rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      .standards-index ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.45rem 1.25rem;
        list-style: none;
      }

      .standards-index a {
        min-height: 2.4rem;
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        font: 550 0.9rem/1.35 var(--sans);
        text-decoration-color: transparent;
        text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
        transition: color 140ms ease, text-decoration-color 140ms ease;
      }

      .standards-index a:hover {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration-color: currentColor;
      }

      .standards-sections {
        padding-bottom: clamp(4rem, 7vw, 7rem);
      }

      .standard-section {
        max-width: 68rem;
        margin-inline: auto;
        padding: clamp(2.8rem, 2.1rem + 2vw, 4.6rem) 0;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 18rem) minmax(0, 41.5rem);
        gap: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 5.5rem);
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        scroll-margin-top: 1rem;
      }

      .standard-section:first-child {
        border-top-color: var(--ink);
      }

      .standard-section__heading h2 {
        max-width: 15ch;
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        font: 630 clamp(1.65rem, 1.2rem + 1.1vw, 2.35rem) / 1.04 var(--sans);
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        text-wrap: balance;
      }

      .standard-section__body {
        min-width: 0;
        font: 400 clamp(1.02rem, 0.98rem + 0.12vw, 1.12rem) / 1.72 var(--serif);
      }

      .standard-section__body > p {
        margin: 0 0 1.35em;
      }

      .standard-section__body > p:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
      }

      .standard-note {
        margin-top: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem);
        padding-top: 0.9rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
      }

      .standard-note > p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      .standard-note > p:not(.standard-note__label) {
        font: 520 1rem/1.55 var(--sans);
      }

      .standard-note__label {
        margin-bottom: 0.65rem !important;
      }

      .standard-note ul,
      .standard-subsection ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 1.15rem;
      }

      .standard-note li,
      .standard-subsection li {
        padding-left: 0.25rem;
      }

      .standard-note li + li,
      .standard-subsection li + li {
        margin-top: 0.35rem;
      }

      .standard-subsection + .standard-subsection {
        margin-top: 2.2rem;
      }

      .standard-subsection h3 {
        margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .standard-note dl {
        margin: 0;
      }

      .standard-note dl > div {
        padding: 0.65rem 0;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        font: 500 0.92rem/1.45 var(--sans);
      }

      .standard-note dt {
        color: var(--muted);
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      }

      .standard-note dd {
        margin: 0;
      }

      @media (max-width: 42rem) {
        .standards-header {
          padding-top: 2.6rem;
        }

        .standards-index {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          gap: 0.65rem;
        }

        .standards-index ul {
          display: grid;
          gap: 0;
        }

        .standards-index li + li {
          border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        }

        .standards-index a {
          min-height: 2.75rem;
          width: 100%;
        }

        .standard-section {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          gap: 1.5rem;
          padding: 2.6rem 0;
        }

        .standard-section__heading h2 {
          max-width: 18ch;
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 28rem) {
        .standards-header h1 {
          font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 11vw, 3.2rem);
        }

        .standards-intro {
          font-size: 1.03rem;
        }

        .standard-note dl > div {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
          gap: 0.2rem;
        }
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        :global(html) {
          scroll-behavior: auto;
        }

        .standards-index a {
          transition: none;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
